    "body": "Hmm. It's not normative text, to my understanding. Regardless, we don't have a convention for citations. I'd be content with something like:\r\n> Per RISC-V ISA, \"...\"\r\n\r\nIf you wanted to put a version of some sort in there, you could, but I don't think it's necessary (and the current versioning of the spec is not the best).\r\n\r\nI wouldn't spend a lot of time on it. I was just trying to understand why this comment's text was in quotation marks. Any sort of clarity there would be fine.",
